WEBVTT
Kind: captions

00:00:00.068 --> 00:00:03.071 position:63%
The people here for training
today are ordinary civilians.

00:00:03.431 --> 00:00:04.532 position:63%
Are the shooters ready?

00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:08.099 position:63%
Attention These civilians
are fathers with families,

00:00:08.439 --> 00:00:11.081 position:63%
IT specialists, bricklayers
and firefighters.

00:00:12.895 --> 00:00:15.877 position:63%
The war in Ukraine pushed
Finland into rearmament.

00:00:16.297 --> 00:00:20.101 position:63%
A lot of people started back in 2022.

00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:25.585 position:63%
I think most of the guys here shooting
today, me especially, started

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:32.436 position:63%
at the time that Russia attacked Ukraine.

00:00:32.437 --> 00:00:34.558 position:63%
Reservists practice their marksmanship.

00:00:41.877 --> 00:00:42.658 position:63%
I think shooting is...

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.362 position:63%
pretty much one of the...

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:55.287 position:63%
most important skills that
a soldier would have.

00:00:55.768 --> 00:01:00.693 position:63%
Every Finnish military
conscript, after they get

00:01:01.333 --> 00:01:04.236 position:63%
their service done, they're
moved into the reserves.

00:01:05.577 --> 00:01:08.400 position:63%
In the event of war, Finland
would be crushed without its

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:12.183 position:63%
reservists, as the country
only has 24,000 professional

00:01:12.263 --> 00:01:15.707 position:63%
soldiers, whereas, for
example, France has 200,000.

00:01:20.021 --> 00:01:22.808 position:63%
Everyone here already knows
what role they would play.

00:01:23.309 --> 00:01:25.415 position:63%
Oli is a computer
scientist at the airport.

00:01:29.116 --> 00:01:34.942 position:63%
My deployment will be at my work, so
I have to go to the airport anyway.

00:01:35.682 --> 00:01:39.766 position:63%
So I will be doing civil
stuff and not military stuff.

00:01:41.428 --> 00:01:42.969 position:63%
Tatu is 52 years old.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:45.031 position:63%
In civilian life, he's a firefighter.

00:01:50.981 --> 00:01:54.904 position:63%
I have to choose because I'm working at a
fire department or I have to go to war.

00:01:55.244 --> 00:01:56.805 position:63%
I, of course, go to war.

00:01:57.085 --> 00:01:58.547 position:63%
And I believe that most of the

00:01:58.807 --> 00:02:04.131 position:63%
Finnish male people think the same.

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.553 position:63%
Is it important to defend the country?

00:02:06.573 --> 00:02:07.273 position:63%
Yes.

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:09.655 position:63%
Our grandfathers did that.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:13.838 position:63%
And if we need to, we do that the same.

00:02:14.719 --> 00:02:19.803 position:63%
Finland will not exist if we are not
doing the same that our grandparents did.

00:02:21.784 --> 00:02:27.112 position:63%
Finns have not forgotten the invasion
of their country by Russia in 1939.

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:35.642 position:63%
Finland's defense makes
it so that it's gonna

00:02:35.742 --> 00:02:39.144 position:63%
be extremely expensive
for Russia to attack.

00:02:39.944 --> 00:02:46.727 position:63%
War is always scary, but being brave
is not about being not scared.

00:02:47.007 --> 00:02:49.168 position:63%
It's about being scared
and still doing stuff.

